  "term": "Sly syndrome",
  "definition": "Sly syndrome is a rare inherited lysosomal storage disease caused by a lack of the enzyme beta-glucuronidase. It is associated with an enlarged liver and spleen, skeletal abnormalities, a larger head, and intellectual disability.",
